# Apiary Design Refresh - Sidebar & Dashboard

## Design System from apiaryeducation.com

### Color Palette
| Name | Hex | Usage |
|------|-----|-------|
| Honey | `#c9944a` | Primary accent, active states, CTAs |
| Honey Light | `#e3b97a` | Hover states |
| Honey Glow | `#f4d4a3` | Subtle highlights |
| Amber | `#a67235` | Darker accent |
| Charcoal | `#1a1a2e` | Sidebar background |
| Slate | `#2d2d44` | Sidebar borders, dividers |
| Cream | `#fef9f3` | Page background |
| Cream Dark | `#f5ede3` | Card backgrounds, table headers |
| Text Dark | `#1a1a2e` | Headings, primary text |
| Text Muted | `#5c5c72` | Secondary text |
| Green | `#22c55e` | Success states |

### Typography
- **Display/Headings**: `'Fraunces'` (serif) - weight 500-600
- **Body/UI**: `'DM Sans'` (sans-serif) - weight 400-600

---

## Implementation Plan

### Step 1: Add Google Fonts
Update both layout files to include Fraunces and DM Sans:
- `Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml` - MVC layout for authenticated pages
- `Components/App.razor` - Blazor layout for forms

### Step 2: Update CSS Variables & Base Styles (`wwwroot/css/site.css`)

**Base styles:**
- Body background: `#f8f9fa` → `#fef9f3` (Cream)
- Add font-family: DM Sans for body, Fraunces for headings
- Auth body background: `#f1f5f9` → `#fef9f3`

**Sidebar styles (lines 38-160):**
- `.sidebar` background: `#1e293b` → `#1a1a2e` (Charcoal)
- `.sidebar-header` border: `#334155` → `#2d2d44` (Slate)
- `.sidebar-nav .nav-link:hover` background: `#334155` → `#2d2d44`
- `.sidebar-nav .nav-link.active` background: `#3b82f6` → `#c9944a` (Honey)
- `.sidebar-footer` border: `#334155` → `#2d2d44`

**Dashboard components:**
- `.stat-value` color: keep `#1e293b` → `#1a1a2e`
- Table header background: `#f8fafc` → `#f5ede3` (Cream Dark)
- Card hover effects: update shadows with honey tint
- Focus ring: `#258cfb` → `#c9944a`

**Page header:**
- `.page-title` color: keep charcoal
- Add Fraunces font for headings

### Step 3: Update Placement Widget Card (`Views/Shared/_CurrentPlacementWidget.cshtml`)
- Stats badge: use honey color for primary stats
- Update `.text-primary` usage to reference honey color
- Card header styling with subtle honey accent

### Step 4: Update Dashboard Quick Links
- Primary buttons: honey-based gradient/color
- Outline buttons: honey border color

---

## Files to Modify

1. **`Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml`** - Add Google Fonts link
2. **`Components/App.razor`** - Add Google Fonts link
3. **`wwwroot/css/site.css`** - Main styling updates:
   - CSS custom properties for colors
   - Typography rules
   - Sidebar color updates
   - Dashboard component updates
4. **`Views/Shared/_CurrentPlacementWidget.cshtml`** - Update stats styling

---

## Preview of Key Changes

### Sidebar (Before → After)
```css
/* Before */
.sidebar { background-color: #1e293b; }
.sidebar-nav .nav-link.active { background-color: #3b82f6; }

/* After */
.sidebar { background-color: #1a1a2e; }
.sidebar-nav .nav-link.active { background-color: #c9944a; }
```

### Body Background
```css
/* Before */
body { background-color: #f8f9fa; }

/* After */
body { background-color: #fef9f3; }
```

### Typography
```css
body { font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; }
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, .page-title { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; }
```
